Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 23:16:45 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] feat(gchat): clarify buttons on by default behind a
 kill-switch; log the text fallback

The clarify card now carries a typed-path hint as well: CARD_CLICKED rides a
Google-side publish leg the gateway can neither observe nor repair, and when
it fails the tap vanishes with no error chip and no log line, while a typed
reply always resolves. platforms.google_chat.clarify_buttons (default true) is
a kill-switch that restores the base-class numbered-text prompt.

The card-to-text fallback that already existed was silent: send_clarify
returns the text prompt's successful result, so a failed card send left no
trace anywhere. It now logs the card error at WARNING first.
