 When the agent asks a multiple-choice clarify question, the adapter renders it
 as a native **Card v2** with one button per choice plus an
 **"Other / type answer"** button, instead of a plain numbered text list.
-Clicking a button answers the question directly (`CARD_CLICKED` events route
-the choice back into the waiting session). If the card fails to send, or the
-question has no fixed choices, the adapter falls back to the standard text
-clarify. No configuration needed.
+Clicking a button answers the question directly: the click travels back
+through the same Pub/Sub subscription (each button names the subscription's
+topic), resolves the waiting session, and the card is patched in place to show
+who answered what. The card also lists the options as text, so a typed reply
+(the number, the option text, or your own answer) works too — that is the
+resilient path, because the click's publish leg is Google-side and can fail
+without any trace on your side. If the card fails to send, or the question has
+no fixed choices, the adapter falls back to the standard text clarify and logs
+the card failure at WARNING.
+
+Buttons are on by default. To switch them off and get plain numbered text
+prompts only, set in `config.yaml`:
+
+```yaml
+platforms:
+  google_chat:
+    clarify_buttons: false
+```
+
+The setting is read once when the adapter starts, so restart the gateway after
+changing it.
 
